diff --git a/docs/priority-init-20261031/README.md b/docs/priority-init-20261031/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2730f34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/priority-init-20261031/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Persistent priority initialization result
+
+The first phone test of automatic app selection used BZJA
+`6.12.69-android16-6-pa4ef354-abogkiS948BXXU5BZJA-4k`. The read-only status was
+`ready=0 configured=0 generation=0 automatic=0 own_appid=0 root_lookup=1`.
+The operator confirmed multiple full reboots, `fail_layer=0`, and the presence of
+`ioprio_check_cap`, `sys_call_table` and `compat_sys_call_table`. No relevant
+printk output was returned. The failure is in priority initialization, before
+automatic list activation; the exact failing step remains unknown.
+
+This diagnostic revision preserves the initialization errno, stage and operation
+after rollback in the existing root-only `priority_filter` status. Stage 1 means
+validation-helper lookup, 2 hook installation, 3 missing compat coverage, and 0
+successful initialization. Operation 0/1/2/3 means getpriority/setpriority/
+ioprio_get/ioprio_set; -1 means no operation. Native/compat masks capture the
+attempt before cleanup; they do not claim that failed hooks remain installed.
+The two entry-instruction words and compat-table presence help distinguish
+landing validation, symbol resolution and table admission. No kernel addresses
+are exposed. The client buffer is extended to 512 bytes.
+
+All hook admission, rollback, lifetime, caller gates, I/O-priority validation and
+automatic selection semantics are unchanged. This revision diagnoses the phone
+failure; it does not claim to repair it. The app no longer presents a generic
+reboot instruction for every unavailable result, and logs the bounded native
+status when readiness/policy checks fail.
+
+Focused production-C priority and control-client runners pass in normal and
+ASan/UBSan configurations. Initialization tests assert retained helper/install/
+compat errors after cleanup and reset on a subsequent successful initialization.
+The ARM64 module/client build and real-header/BZJA static checks also pass.
+These checks do not execute kernel hooks or establish phone compatibility.
